From: TrickFire Robotics <trickfire@uw.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] SCMTerrain: drop the default active domain on first user domain

SetupInitial() installs one active domain with a null body. AddActiveDomain()
appended to that list without clearing it, so OnBindAssets() later iterated a
domain whose body was null and dereferenced it.

Clearing the list the first time a user domain is added keeps the default
behaviour intact while making AddActiveDomain() safe to call.

Reported upstream; remove this patch once a Chrono release contains the fix.
---
 src/chrono_vehicle/terrain/SCMTerrain.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/chrono_vehicle/terrain/SCMTerrain.cpp b/src/chrono_vehicle/terrain/SCMTerrain.cpp
index fb6d6be..7386379 100644
--- a/src/chrono_vehicle/terrain/SCMTerrain.cpp
+++ b/src/chrono_vehicle/terrain/SCMTerrain.cpp
@@ -229,6 +229,8 @@ void SCMTerrain::AddActiveDomain(std::shared_ptr<ChBody> body, const ChVector3d&
     ad.m_center = OOBB_center;
     ad.m_hdims = OOBB_dims / 2;
 
+    if (!m_loader->m_user_domains)
+        m_loader->m_active_domains.clear();
     m_loader->m_active_domains.push_back(ad);
 
     // Enable user-provided active domains
